-- Integration — an external connector: type + credentials + config +
-- enabled flag.
--
-- Static rows: none. Lives in a dedicated `integrations` SQL table —
-- registered here purely for the validation surface. Identity is lifted
-- from the directives below; the auto-register loop registers it. The
-- pre-flip inline-TS `defineSystemEntity` is GONE.
--
-- FM-retire-E1 Step 6 — id ships LOWERCASE via `@codeName "integration"`.
-- NB the `config: Maybe ({})` field: the `{}` empty-record literal is a
-- COMPOUND type-app arg, so it needs parens at constructor-field position
-- (`Maybe {}` parses `{}` as a separate positional field) — the same
-- paren convention as `Maybe (EntityRef<"item">)` in profile_intent /
-- `List (List GeoPoint)` in country. `credentials: {}` (bare, non-Maybe)
-- needs no parens. `enabled: Maybe Boolean` uses `Boolean` (the opaque
-- True|False entity), distinct from `Bool` — preserved verbatim.

@entity
@codeName "integration"
@label "Integration"
@description "External connector — type + credentials + config + enabled flag"
@icon "plug"
Integration = Integration type: String label: Maybe String credentials: {} config: Maybe ({}) enabled: Maybe Boolean
